{"id": "EUVD-2025-211116", "enisaUuid": "88b23c07-2a0a-349c-a137-24951a1c834d", "description": "The ForgeRock client fails to correctly validate refresh tokens. This allows a refresh token to be treated as a valid access token, enabling its use for consuming protected resources. This bypasses the intended security control that requires valid client credentials in addition to a refresh token to obtain a new access token.\n\nAn attacker who obtains a stolen or exposed refresh token can leverage this vulnerability to directly access protected resources. This is possible because the standard security flow requiring client credentials to exchange a refresh token for an access token is circumvented.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T16:28:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:28:15", "baseScore": 5.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://security.docs.wso2.com/en/latest/security-announcements/security-advisories/2026/WSO2-2025-4337/"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vp4v-gjpc-c4x6", "CVE-2025-7043"], "assigner": "WSO2", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "128feea9-7c0e-33e9-a2be-5c5cd0049e77", "product": {"name": "Forgerock Key Manager Component", "vendor": {"name": "WSO2"}}, "product_version": "1.0.0 <1.0.0.3"}, {"id": "33523f18-47bb-3763-9e70-23911fe102d8", "product": {"name": "WSO2 API Manager", "vendor": {"name": "WSO2"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0 <4.2.0.156"}, {"id": "3e898179-c7cd-3e1a-bc13-502cca01c278", "product": {"name": "Forgerock Key Manager Component", "vendor": {"name": "WSO2"}}, "product_version": "1.1.5 <1.1.5.4"}, {"id": "47938119-e8cf-36ce-a220-ee5c62fa69b9", "product": {"name": "WSO2 API Manager", "vendor": {"name": "WSO2"}}, "product_version": "4.3.0 <4.3.0.67"}, {"id": "4c7ba824-3e06-32cc-ab2d-94b929acad11", "product": {"name": "WSO2 API Manager", "vendor": {"name": "WSO2"}}, "product_version": "4.4.0 <4.4.0.30"}, {"id": "4dabaab0-c587-308e-87c3-6670be987f80", "product": {"name": "WSO